Falsifies `pci::verification::the_capability_walk_terminates_on_any_device`.

The defect: the hop bound is one too many, `0..65` in place of `0..64`. The walk still
terminates, so the property a reader checks first survives; what breaks is the exact bound the
callback contract states, and a caller sizing a buffer by that bound overruns it by one entry.
An off-by-one in a loop count is the error this shape invites, and no fixture device has a
64-entry capability list.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(calls <= 64)`, on a cyclic capability list, at 65
callbacks. The harness's `#[kani::unwind(66)]` still covers the loop, so this is a property
failure and not an unwinding-assertion failure; that distinction is the thing to check if this
patch ever reports something else.

